From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NuxFX <nuxfx@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 21:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 28/28] dzn: do not make workgroup barriers coherent

A DirectML kernel of the machine learning models of After Effects 26 (Roto
Brush) has 33 barriers at workgroup scope that make memory available and
visible (the Vulkan memory model, as vkd3d-proton emits it for
GroupMemoryBarrierWithGroupSync). nir_lower_memory_model made every group
shared access around them coherent, and dxil_nir_lower_coherent_loads_and_stores
turned each of those into an atomic exchange or add: 128 atomics on group
shared memory in the one kernel. The Direct3D 12 driver of an NVIDIA GPU
crashes while it compiles that DXIL (a null pointer in the driver's
CreateComputePipelineState), and with it After Effects.

A barrier whose memory scope is the workgroup or narrower is already satisfied
by the DXIL group barrier with its group shared and thread group UAV fences.
The availability and visibility bits of such a barrier are dropped before
nir_lower_memory_model, so the accesses stay plain loads and stores. Barriers
of wider scope keep their semantics.
---
diff --git a/src/microsoft/spirv_to_dxil/dxil_spirv_nir.c b/src/microsoft/spirv_to_dxil/dxil_spirv_nir.c
--- a/src/microsoft/spirv_to_dxil/dxil_spirv_nir.c
+++ b/src/microsoft/spirv_to_dxil/dxil_spirv_nir.c
@@ -576,6 +576,29 @@
    return true;
 }
 
+/* A barrier at workgroup scope or narrower that makes memory available or visible is already
+ * satisfied by the DXIL group barrier with its group shared and thread group UAV fences. Left as
+ * it is, nir_lower_memory_model turns every access around such a barrier into a coherent one and
+ * dxil_nir_lower_coherent_loads_and_stores turns those into atomics: one atomic per group shared
+ * load or store (128 of them in one DirectML kernel), which the Direct3D 12 driver of an
+ * NVIDIA GPU cannot compile (the driver crashes in CreateComputePipelineState). */
+static bool
+drop_narrow_scope_available_visible(nir_builder *b, nir_intrinsic_instr *intrin,
+                                    void *cb_data)
+{
+   if (intrin->intrinsic != nir_intrinsic_barrier ||
+       nir_intrinsic_memory_scope(intrin) > SCOPE_WORKGROUP)
+      return false;
+
+   const nir_memory_semantics drop = NIR_MEMORY_MAKE_AVAILABLE | NIR_MEMORY_MAKE_VISIBLE;
+   nir_memory_semantics semantics = nir_intrinsic_memory_semantics(intrin);
+   if (!(semantics & drop))
+      return false;
+
+   nir_intrinsic_set_memory_semantics(intrin, semantics & ~drop);
+   return true;
+}
+
 struct lower_pntc_data {
    const struct dxil_spirv_runtime_conf *conf;
    nir_variable *pntc;
@@ -982,6 +1005,8 @@
       NIR_PASS_V(nir, nir_zero_initialize_shared_memory,
                   nir->info.shared_size, 4);
    }
+   NIR_PASS_V(nir, nir_shader_intrinsics_pass, drop_narrow_scope_available_visible,
+              nir_metadata_all, NULL);
    NIR_PASS_V(nir, nir_lower_memory_model);
    NIR_PASS_V(nir, dxil_nir_lower_coherent_loads_and_stores);
 
